Register dlls/lsteamclient with stock Wine 11.0's build system, for the Sikarugir runner.

The same registration as register-components.diff, against the tree Sikarugir's 11.0
engine is built from. programs/steam.exe is left out: 11.0 has neither WINE_EXTERNAL nor
the PE libc++ that CXX_PE_LIBS names, both of which arrived after it, so the shim is
built from the 11.15 tree instead. It is a PE program that only imports Win32 DLLs, so
its build does not have to match the runner's ntdll the way lsteamclient's unix half does.

11.0's makedep also has no parser for .cpp, so it never sees the "#pragma makedep unix"
in Valve's C++ sources and builds all 219 of them into the PE halves, where they fail.
Parsing .cpp as C is what later makedep does, and it is enough for the pragma to land.
The unix half is still compiled by lsteamclient/build.sh, not by make.

